 "frozen_rule": "Frozen before replay (2026-10-26T07:21Z).\nChange under test: opt-in --max-fixed-doppler-consensus-age <s> (branch fix/rtk-doppler-consensus-expiry on develop afa214ab;\nbinary bin/gnss-solve-dexp). Without the flag, default and CDM POS are byte-identical to develop (Odaiba checked).\nValue: 5 s = the CD recipe's existing --max-fixed-anchor-age; not tuned (Odaiba CDM track error p95 0.5 m at 2-5 s,\nD rejected nothing below 30 s and 2703 correct vs 1 wrong candidates at >= 30 s).\nRecipes: default; CDM = CD + M; CDME = CDM + --max-fixed-doppler-consensus-age 5.\nPPC bare argv as docs/rtk_cdmh_ppc_evaluation.md; PPC profile P as docs/rtk_cd_ppc_profile.md (P, P+CDM, P+CDME).\nBaseline for the user goal: RTKLIB demo5 b34k 55a0f2c with scripts/rtklib_odaiba.conf (pos1-navsys=61), surveyed base on\nTokyo (-r), header base on PPC.\nRuns: Trimble Odaiba/Shinjuku, u-blox Odaiba/Shinjuku, PPC tokyo/nagoya run1-3 (bare + P), HK Deep/Harsh (descriptive).\nReference only for scoring.\nPrediction (mechanism): CDME recovers most of CDM's consensus lock-out: on Trimble Odaiba CDME FIX > 5839 (RTKLIB) and\nwrong FIX >0.5 m <= 19 (RTKLIB); P+CDME P-correct loss falls below 20% on every PPC run (P+CDM: 58-89%).\nGates (each per run):\n C (effect of E, CDME vs CDM): wrong FIX >0.5/2/3 m not increased; CDM-correct loss <= 1%; missing and horizontal P95\n   not increased. Pass on every run -> keep E as an opt-in fix of the D gate and add it to the CD-family recipe docs.\n A (user goal, CDME vs RTKLIB demo5 multi-GNSS, same matching 0.11 s for both): more FIX epochs AND wrong FIX\n   >0.5/2/3 m each <= RTKLIB. Reported per run; claims only where it holds.\n B (docs/fix_recovery_guard.md vs default, incl. decrease clause): reported; expected to fail as for CDM.\nNo default change in this round. No retuning after the replay.\n",
